{"request":{"path":"/rest/contents/search","query":{"limit":1,"offset":0,"projection":"full","sort":"visualSimilarity:desc"},"body":{"operator":"and","filters":{"format":{"includes":["video"]},"publishedAt":{"after":"2026-06-27","before":"2026-09-27"},"visualSimilarity":{"includes":{"values":[{"assetId":"ast_pNv2qCvwlS0H5JDnMgB9bK3YOCqZ","minScore":0.8}]}}},"queries":[{"operator":"or","filters":{"caption":{"includesExactly":{"values":["running","runner","marathon"],"operator":"or"}}}}]}},"status":206,"fetchedAt":"2026-09-27T07:32:35.226Z","response":{"data":{"aggregations":{"totalViewsCount":110796862,"totalInteractionsCount":3247624,"totalEngagementRatePerViews":0.02931151606080685,"totalEngagementRatePerFollowers":0.009575581779372313},"results":[{"id":"cnt_278eb8f9abc0437cf8ec608b8aff","matchedQueries":[],"platform":"instagram","profileHandle":"nicofelich","profileDisplayName":"Nico Felich","format":"video","caption":"The Best Running Gear in 2026 (in my opinion)\n\n#running #runner #marathon #marathontraining #recommendations","captionLanguage":"de","thumbnailMediaId":"med_8bbf1d99243df9775b5684ccd0ea","publishedAt":"2026-06-29T19:11:26.000Z","profileId":"prf_5fec4dc01496a44dd663acecc5e7","thumbnailMediaUrl":"https://oriane-contents.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/instagram/DaLlZKls2qR/thumbnail.webp","viewsCount":1119523,"likesCount":47227,"sharesCount":10608,"commentsCount":186,"interactionsCount":58021,"engagementRatePerViews":5.182653683756386,"engagementRatePerFollowers":22.722857970878273,"profileFollowersCount":255342,"profileFollowingCount":862,"profilePostsCount":482,"mediaCount":1,"duration":107.4,"hashtags":["#running","#runner","#marathon","#marathontraining","#recommendations"],"coAuthors":[],"mentions":[],"platformId":"DaLlZKls2qR","profilePlatformId":"49957334","profilePictureUrl":"https://oriane-handles.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/instagram/nicofelich/pfp.webp","profileBio":"I love running and making videos about running\n@bpnsupps athlete","profileVerified":true,"locationPlatformId":null,"locationCompleteAddress":null,"locationLatitude":null,"locationLongitude":null,"profileLocationPlatformId":null,"profileLocationCompleteAddress":null,"profileLocationLatitude":null,"profileLocationLongitude":null,"transcript":"This is all the best running gear you can buy in 2026. So many different brands make great running gear, but here are the things I actually use and recommend as a runner. All right, sunglasses. I recommend the Oakley Radar EVs. These look awesome. They're super comfortable and they don't bounce when you're running. I also recommend the Oakley eye jackets. Same thing. They fit super comfortable on your face. A more affordable option that looks similar are the Rendezvous R3s. Good running headphones are super important to me. The Beats Powerbeats Pro 2s have the all-around best fit and sound quality. I've also been loving the Shox Open Dots. Not quite as good sound quality, but still really good. The Shox Open Run Pro 2s are great if you want to feel more aware and have more of an open ear feel. The DSG Quarter Crew socks have and probably always will be my favorite running socks. Then in second place come the Nike Unicorn socks. All right, now the fun stuff, shoes. I have tested all of these extensively. Here are my recommendations. For an affordable daily trainer, New Balance Ellipse. Another well-priced daily trainer are the Adidas Evo SL. My favorite daily trainer to date are the Nike Vomero Plus. For race day or workout shoes, Nike Alpha Fly 3s, Hoka CLO 3s, Adidas Adios Pro 4s, which are probably my favorite race day shoes. And then finally, Saucony Endorphin Elite 3s. If you're a shorts person, my favorite are the Satisfy Spaceo shorts, but they're really expensive. A more affordable option are the New Balance RC shorts. Lululemon Fast and Free shorts are good. And then of course, Nike Trail. I mostly wear half tights. The ones I recommend most are the Lululemon Fast and Free. These will genuinely change your life. Pretty much every brand makes a good running shirt. Just make sure it's lightweight and breathable. My favorite shirts are definitely Satisfy, but they're very expensive. If you're feeling bold, the Nike Radical Airflow shirt is pretty crazy. The two hats I recommend are the CLA hats and the Aloe hats. The CLA 5 panel hat is very flexible and comfortable. And same thing with the Aloe Performance hat. I love this thing. The watch I use is the Garmin 4Runner 970. If you want a more affordable option, use the Coro Space Pro. I wear the Whoop 5.0. I can't sleep with my Garmin, but I can sleep with my Whoop, and it tracks everything I do 24-7. My most essential running supplements are BPN Go gels and BPN electrolytes. And then lastly, for recovery, I recommend the Norma Tech boots.","transcriptLanguage":"en","transcriptChunks":[{"startSeconds":0.005,"endSeconds":2.645,"text":"This is all the best running gear you can buy in 2026."},{"startSeconds":2.645,"endSeconds":6.245,"text":"So many different brands make great running gear, but here are the things I actually use"},{"startSeconds":6.245,"endSeconds":10.565,"text":"and recommend as a runner. All right, sunglasses. I recommend the Oakley Radar EVs. These look"},{"startSeconds":10.565,"endSeconds":13.605,"text":"awesome. They're super comfortable and they don't bounce when you're running. I also recommend the"},{"startSeconds":13.605,"endSeconds":17.045,"text":"Oakley eye jackets. Same thing. They fit super comfortable on your face. A more affordable"},{"startSeconds":17.045,"endSeconds":21.125,"text":"option that looks similar are the Rendezvous R3s. Good running headphones are super important to me."},{"startSeconds":21.125,"endSeconds":25.285,"text":"The Beats Powerbeats Pro 2s have the all-around best fit and sound quality. I've also been loving"},{"startSeconds":25.285,"endSeconds":28.965,"text":"the Shox Open Dots. Not quite as good sound quality, but still really good. The Shox Open"},{"startSeconds":28.965,"endSeconds":33.285,"text":"Run Pro 2s are great if you want to feel more aware and have more of an open ear feel. The DSG"},{"startSeconds":33.285,"endSeconds":37.205,"text":"Quarter Crew socks have and probably always will be my favorite running socks. Then in second place"},{"startSeconds":37.205,"endSeconds":42.085,"text":"come the Nike Unicorn socks. All right, now the fun stuff, shoes. I have tested all of these extensively."},{"startSeconds":42.085,"endSeconds":45.765,"text":"Here are my recommendations. For an affordable daily trainer, New Balance Ellipse. Another"},{"startSeconds":45.765,"endSeconds":50.165,"text":"well-priced daily trainer are the Adidas Evo SL. My favorite daily trainer to date are the Nike"},{"startSeconds":50.165,"endSeconds":56.245,"text":"Vomero Plus. For race day or workout shoes, Nike Alpha Fly 3s, Hoka CLO 3s, Adidas Adios Pro 4s,"},{"startSeconds":56.245,"endSeconds":59.845,"text":"which are probably my favorite race day shoes. And then finally, Saucony Endorphin Elite 3s."},{"startSeconds":59.845,"endSeconds":63.125,"text":"If you're a shorts person, my favorite are the Satisfy Spaceo shorts, but they're really expensive."},{"startSeconds":63.125,"endSeconds":67.365,"text":"A more affordable option are the New Balance RC shorts. Lululemon Fast and Free shorts are good."},{"startSeconds":67.365,"endSeconds":71.045,"text":"And then of course, Nike Trail. I mostly wear half tights. The ones I recommend most are the"},{"startSeconds":71.045,"endSeconds":74.725,"text":"Lululemon Fast and Free. These will genuinely change your life. Pretty much every brand makes"},{"startSeconds":74.725,"endSeconds":77.845,"text":"a good running shirt. Just make sure it's lightweight and breathable. My favorite shirts are"},{"startSeconds":77.845,"endSeconds":81.765,"text":"definitely Satisfy, but they're very expensive. If you're feeling bold, the Nike Radical Airflow"},{"startSeconds":81.765,"endSeconds":86.645,"text":"shirt is pretty crazy. The two hats I recommend are the CLA hats and the Aloe hats. The CLA 5 panel"},{"startSeconds":86.645,"endSeconds":90.565,"text":"hat is very flexible and comfortable. And same thing with the Aloe Performance hat. I love this"},{"startSeconds":90.565,"endSeconds":94.565,"text":"thing. The watch I use is the Garmin 4Runner 970. If you want a more affordable option, use the"},{"startSeconds":94.565,"endSeconds":98.725,"text":"Coro Space Pro. I wear the Whoop 5.0. I can't sleep with my Garmin, but I can sleep with my Whoop,"},{"startSeconds":98.725,"endSeconds":103.605,"text":"and it tracks everything I do 24-7. My most essential running supplements are BPN Go gels and BPN"},{"startSeconds":103.605,"endSeconds":116.485,"text":"electrolytes. And then lastly, for recovery, I recommend the Norma Tech boots."}],"frames":[{"id":"med_fd82101dafcd024d183780c6a055","position":1,"timestampSeconds":2.73,"url":"https://oriane-frames.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/instagram/DaLlZKls2qR/1_2.73.webp"},{"id":"med_39614c8961c46b00c71b7d1e3402","position":2,"timestampSeconds":2.77,"url":"https://oriane-frames.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/instagram/DaLlZKls2qR/2_2.77.webp"},{"id":"med_a975d2beff92fecc4f0612d4addf","position":3,"timestampSeconds":5.37,"url":"https://oriane-frames.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/instagram/DaLlZKls2qR/3_5.37.webp"},{"id":"med_3b27a3c09c9fdb9dd39ec835fc9e","position":4,"timestampSeconds":7.6,"url":"https://oriane-frames.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/instagram/DaLlZKls2qR/4_7.60.webp"},{"id":"med_0da93a69d4f2231c578196a95748","position":5,"timestampSeconds":8.33,"url":"https://oriane-frames.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/instagram/DaLlZKls2qR/5_8.33.webp"},{"id":"med_fe936d364bca38dc11bd5c737d56","position":6,"timestampSeconds":10.33,"url":"https://oriane-frames.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/instagram/DaLlZKls2qR/6_10.33.webp"},{"id":"med_4f1e71461e431da01272a4d64b91","position":7,"timestampSeconds":10.37,"url":"https://oriane-frames.s3.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/instagram/DaLlZ